win32: export the kernel32 functions the bundled kernel32.def already carried

The committed lib/kernel32.def was extended by hand over the years with
exports that V's own library calls and that the pinned tinycc base does
not export: CreateHardLinkW and GetFinalPathNameByHandleW (os),
GetNativeSystemInfo (builtin), K32GetProcessMemoryInfo (runtime), and the
condition-variable trio InitializeConditionVariable,
SleepConditionVariableSRW and WakeConditionVariable (sync), plus
GetConsoleWindow, GetCurrentProcessorNumber and the narrow
GetFinalPathNameByHandle.

build.ps1 now copies tinycc's win32/lib/kernel32.def over the bundled copy,
so without this patch a rebuild silently drops those ten exports and a
program that imports os or sync fails to link under tcc with "unresolved
reference". Add them to the source definition file in sorted order, so the
rebuilt and the committed kernel32.def are the same file.
diff --git a/win32/lib/kernel32.def b/win32/lib/kernel32.def
index a53c0f66..206967b6 100644
--- a/win32/lib/kernel32.def
+++ b/win32/lib/kernel32.def
@@ -75,6 +75,7 @@ CreateFileA
 CreateFileMappingA
